    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="0536" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 422.11 G93/480.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 29, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Railway company controller now has draft of Minister of Hacienda for 57,230
                    sucres. The Minister has instructed Amsinck to pay railway company through
                    Consul General, New York, 28,770 sucres. Controller has draft on said Consul
                    General 14,000 sucres. Total, 100,000.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
